{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "5f89820f-3450-83b0-af5a-c5ea7024022a",
  "created_at": "2026-01-06T11:18:13-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Frank Iannuccilli",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tony Ferreira",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:16:09-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Tony. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:16:13-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, hi Tony. Frank Iannuccilli. I got a water bill here and it's wicked high, and it doesn't make any sense."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:16:20-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, let's take a look. Do you have the account number in front of you, or the service address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:16:26-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I got the bill, yeah. Hang on. Now, I got two places, see, so this might be the other one. Hold on. [pause] No, this is the one I rent. The one I own is the other bill. I always mix 'em up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:16:39-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. Read me the account number off the one that looks high."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:16:44-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's, uh, the one that says forty-one on the top, ending in seven seven two."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:16:49-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. I'm showing the usage for the last quarter is up quite a bit from the one before."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:16:55-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's what I'm saying. I was away six weeks. Gone, nobody in the place, water off at the faucets. How do I use more water when I'm not even there?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:17:05-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, a few things can do it. A running toilet or a small leak will rack up usage even when nobody's home. Also the reading can be an estimate and then catch up. Was it a real reading or an estimate, that's what I'll check."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:17:19-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Eh, I don't know. Check it, please. It's aggravating, I'm paying for water I never touched."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:17:25-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. I'll flag it for a meter re-read and someone will call you back. Is this a good number, the one you're on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:17:33-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-nine-five. Now listen, I'm leaving on another trip Thursday. How do I pay this without coming down to City Hall? Is there a way when you're closed, like online or a box or something?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:17:45-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure. You can pay online through the city website anytime, day or night. There's also a drop box outside City Hall for checks, and you can mail it in too."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:17:55-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, the box is good. I'll drop a check Wednesday. And I gotta go, I got choir stuff. The school choir does the holiday program on the fifteenth and I'm helping set up."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:18:06-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, that sounds nice. I'll get that re-read request in today, Mr. Iannuccilli."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-06T11:18:11-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thanks, Tony. Appreciate it."
    }
  ],
